course: dictionary
lesson: 14861
title: Rationing: sharing what there is
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rationing means sharing something out in small, fixed amounts because there is not enough for everyone. Look at the clues around the word. «During the war, every family had a ration book.» If there is not enough food, the government must limit how much each person can have, so the book tells you how much is allowed.
explain: Rationing can be about food, fuel, clothes, or anything that must last. «The sailors were on water rationing, with one small cup each day.» Here the sailors cannot have as much water as they want, so each person gets a fixed share.
explain: A ration is one fixed share. «Each person gets a ration of sugar each week.» Ration is a noun, and rationing is the whole system of sharing things out this way. To check, swap in your meaning: "The government limited how much food each person could have" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Rationing means sharing something out in small, fixed amounts so that it lasts.
fact: «Rationing» is the -ing form of the verb «ration», which can also be used as a noun.
fact: In Britain during and after the Second World War, food, fuel and clothes were rationed.
fact: Families used ration books with coupons for things like butter, sugar, meat and eggs.
fact: Sweet rationing in Britain ended in 1953.
exercise: In the war, families had to share food in fixed amounts. What is this system called? | Feasting | *Rationing | Shopping | Saving money
exercise: «The sailors had to ration their water, one small cup each day.» What does ration mean here? | To throw the water away | To fill the boat with water | *To share out in small, fixed amounts | To drink as much as they like
exercise: «20 biscuits were rationed over 5 days.» How many biscuits can be eaten each day? | 3 | 2 | 5 | *4
test: «Dad's ration book had coupons for butter.» What is a ration book for? | *To show how much food each person may buy | To keep a diary | To read stories | To count money
test: Which sentence shows rationing? | The children played outside all day | We had a picnic in the park | Mum baked a cake for everyone | *The shop lets each family buy only two eggs a week because there are not enough
exam: Dad says, «Each person gets a ration of sugar each week.» What does ration mean here? | A rude way of speaking | A kind of cake | *A fixed share of something | A shop that sells sugar
